-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: Subchapter V (stock and dividends), sections 162 to 166
-- (stock not paid in full, calls, forfeiture, and subscriptions).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The seat layer is dg3-seat.l4.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550),
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Sections 162 to 166 are among those that section 114(b)(2) takes out of the stockholder-to-member reading of section 114(a).
-- Periods of days, weeks, months and years are counted with dg-core's `the date` ... `after` / `before`, and the last day of a period is inside it (Fork F10 in NOTES.md).
-- Out of range: section 325 (dg10: how the sum is recovered after a writ of execution).

§ `Section 162: liability of stockholder or subscriber for stock not paid in full`

-- Section 162(a): when the whole consideration for shares has not been paid in and the assets are insufficient to satisfy the claims of creditors,
-- each holder of or subscriber for such shares is bound to pay, on each share, the sum necessary to complete the unpaid balance of the consideration.
-- src:547 | When the whole of the consideration payable for shares of a corporation has not been paid in, and the assets shall be insufficient to satisfy the claims of its creditors, each holder of or subscriber for such shares shall be bound to pay on each share held or subscribed for by such holder or subscriber the sum necessary to complete the amount of the unpaid balance of the consideration for which such shares were issued or are to be issued by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(a) (src:547)
GIVEN `the whole of the consideration payable for the shares has not been paid in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assets are insufficient to satisfy the claims of the creditors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(a) the holder of or subscriber for the shares is bound to pay the unpaid balance` `the whole of the consideration payable for the shares has not been paid in` `the assets are insufficient to satisfy the claims of the creditors of the corporation` MEANS
        `the whole of the consideration payable for the shares has not been paid in`
    AND `the assets are insufficient to satisfy the claims of the creditors of the corporation`

-- src:547 | each holder of or subscriber for such shares shall be bound to pay on each share held or subscribed for by such holder or subscriber the sum necessary to complete the amount of the unpaid balance of the consideration for which such shares were issued or are to be issued by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(a) (src:547)
GIVEN `the number of shares held or subscribed for` IS A NUMBER
      `the unpaid balance of the consideration on each share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 162(a) the sum the holder or subscriber is bound to pay` `the number of shares held or subscribed for` `the unpaid balance of the consideration on each share` MEANS
    `the number of shares held or subscribed for` TIMES `the unpaid balance of the consideration on each share`

-- Section 162(b): the amounts payable under (a) may be recovered as provided in section 325, after a writ of execution against the corporation has been returned unsatisfied as provided there.
-- src:548 | The amounts which shall be payable as provided in subsection (a) of this section may be recovered as provided in § 325 of this title, after a writ of execution against the corporation has been returned unsatisfied as provided in said § 325.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(b) (src:548)
GIVEN `the holder or subscriber is bound to pay under subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 325 (piece dg10)
      `a writ of execution against the corporation has been returned unsatisfied as provided in section 325` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(b) the amount payable may be recovered as provided in section 325` `the holder or subscriber is bound to pay under subsection (a)` `a writ of execution against the corporation has been returned unsatisfied as provided in section 325` MEANS
        `the holder or subscriber is bound to pay under subsection (a)`
    AND `a writ of execution against the corporation has been returned unsatisfied as provided in section 325`

-- Section 162(c): a person who becomes an assignee or transferee of shares or of a subscription in good faith and without knowledge or notice that the full consideration has not been paid
-- is not personally liable for any unpaid portion, but the transferor remains liable. The text does not say who is liable when the transferee is not so protected: NOTHING.
-- src:549 | Any person becoming an assignee or transferee of shares or of a subscription for shares in good faith and without knowledge or notice that the full consideration therefor has not been paid shall not be personally liable for any unpaid portion of such consideration, but the transferor shall remain liable therefor.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(c) (src:549)
GIVEN `the person became an assignee or transferee of the shares or of a subscription in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became one without knowledge or notice that the full consideration has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(c) the assignee or transferee is not personally liable for the unpaid portion` `the person became an assignee or transferee of the shares or of a subscription in good faith` `the person became one without knowledge or notice that the full consideration has not been paid` MEANS
        `the person became an assignee or transferee of the shares or of a subscription in good faith`
    AND `the person became one without knowledge or notice that the full consideration has not been paid`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(c) (src:549)
GIVEN `the assignee or transferee is not personally liable under subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(c) the transferor remains liable for the unpaid portion` `the assignee or transferee is not personally liable under subsection (c)` MEANS
    IF `the assignee or transferee is not personally liable under subsection (c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 162(d): a person holding shares as collateral security is not personally liable as a stockholder, but the person pledging them is considered the holder and is so liable;
-- an executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary is not personally liable as a stockholder, but the estate or funds held in that capacity are liable.
-- src:550 | No person holding shares in any corporation as collateral security shall be personally liable as a stockholder but the person pledging such shares shall be considered the holder thereof and shall be so liable. No executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary shall be personally liable as a stockholder, but the estate or funds held by such executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary in such fiduciary capacity shall be liable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(d) (src:550)
DECLARE `s 162(d) The capacity in which a person holds shares` IS ONE OF
    `as collateral security under s 162(d)`
    `as an executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary under s 162(d)`
    `in another capacity under s 162(d)`

-- src:550 | No executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary shall be personally liable as a stockholder, but the estate or funds held by such executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary in such fiduciary capacity shall be liable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(d) (src:550)
GIVEN capacity IS A `s 162(d) The capacity in which a person holds shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(d) the person holding the shares is personally liable as a stockholder` capacity MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `as collateral security under s 162(d)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `as an executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary under s 162(d)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `in another capacity under s 162(d)` THEN NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(d) (src:550)
GIVEN capacity IS A `s 162(d) The capacity in which a person holds shares`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(d) the person pledging the shares is considered the holder and is liable as a stockholder` capacity MEANS
    capacity EQUALS `as collateral security under s 162(d)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(d) (src:550)
GIVEN capacity IS A `s 162(d) The capacity in which a person holds shares`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(d) the estate or funds held in the fiduciary capacity are liable` capacity MEANS
    capacity EQUALS `as an executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary under s 162(d)`

-- Section 162(e): no liability under section 162 or section 325 shall be asserted more than 6 years after the issuance of the stock or the date of the subscription upon which the assessment is sought.
-- src:551 | No liability under this section or under § 325 of this title shall be asserted more than 6 years after the issuance of the stock or the date of the subscription upon which the assessment is sought.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(e) (src:551)
GIVEN `the day of the issuance of the stock or the date of the subscription upon which the assessment is sought` IS A DATE
      `the day the liability is asserted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(e) the liability may be asserted` `the day of the issuance of the stock or the date of the subscription upon which the assessment is sought` `the day the liability is asserted` MEANS
    `the day the liability is asserted` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in years` 6) `after` `the day of the issuance of the stock or the date of the subscription upon which the assessment is sought`)

-- Section 162(f): in any action by a receiver or trustee of an insolvent corporation, or by a judgment creditor, to obtain an assessment under the section,
-- any stockholder or subscriber for stock of the insolvent corporation may appear and contest the claim or claims.
-- src:552 | In any action by a receiver or trustee of an insolvent corporation or by a judgment creditor to obtain an assessment under this section, any stockholder or subscriber for stock of the insolvent corporation may appear and contest the claim or claims of such receiver or trustee.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 162(f) (src:552)
GIVEN `the action is by a receiver or trustee of an insolvent corporation or by a judgment creditor to obtain an assessment under section 162` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a stockholder or subscriber for stock of the insolvent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(f) the stockholder or subscriber may appear and contest the claim` `the action is by a receiver or trustee of an insolvent corporation or by a judgment creditor to obtain an assessment under section 162` `the person is a stockholder or subscriber for stock of the insolvent corporation` MEANS
        `the action is by a receiver or trustee of an insolvent corporation or by a judgment creditor to obtain an assessment under section 162`
    AND `the person is a stockholder or subscriber for stock of the insolvent corporation`

§ `Section 163: payment for stock not paid in full`

-- The capital stock is paid for in such amounts and at such times as the directors may require. The directors may from time to time demand, on each share not fully paid,
-- such sum as the necessities of the business may, in the judgment of the board, require, not exceeding in the whole the balance remaining unpaid on the stock.
-- Whether the necessities of the business require the sum is the board's judgment: an input.
-- src:556 | The directors may, from time to time, demand payment, in respect of each share of stock not fully paid, of such sum of money as the necessities of the business may, in the judgment of the board of directors, require, not exceeding in the whole the balance remaining unpaid on said stock, and such sum so demanded shall be paid to the corporation at such times and by such installments as the directors shall direct. The directors shall give notice of the time and place of such payments, which notice shall be given at least 30 days before the time for such payment, to each holder of or subscriber for stock which is not fully paid at such holder’s or subscriber’s last known address.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 163 (src:556)
GIVEN `the board of directors judges that the necessities of the business require the sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sums demanded in the whole on each share` IS A NUMBER
      `the balance remaining unpaid on each share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 163 the directors may demand the payment` `the board of directors judges that the necessities of the business require the sum` `the sums demanded in the whole on each share` `the balance remaining unpaid on each share` MEANS
        `the board of directors judges that the necessities of the business require the sum`
    AND (`the sums demanded in the whole on each share` AT MOST `the balance remaining unpaid on each share`)

-- The directors shall give notice of the time and place of the payment, at least 30 days before the time for it, to each holder of or subscriber for stock which is not fully paid, at the last known address.
-- src:556 | The directors shall give notice of the time and place of such payments, which notice shall be given at least 30 days before the time for such payment, to each holder of or subscriber for stock which is not fully paid at such holder’s or subscriber’s last known address.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 163 (src:556)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day set for the payment` IS A DATE
      `the notice states the time and place of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given to each holder of or subscriber for stock which is not fully paid, at the last known address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 163 the notice of the payment is as the section requires` `the day the notice was given` `the day set for the payment` `the notice states the time and place of the payment` `the notice was given to each holder of or subscriber for stock which is not fully paid, at the last known address` MEANS
        `the notice states the time and place of the payment`
    AND `the notice was given to each holder of or subscriber for stock which is not fully paid, at the last known address`
    AND (`the day the notice was given` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `before` `the day set for the payment`))

§ `Section 164: failure to pay for stock; remedies`

-- When a stockholder fails to pay an installment or call on the stockholder's stock, properly demanded by the directors, when it is due, the directors may collect it by an action at law,
-- or they shall sell at public sale such part of the delinquent stockholder's shares as will pay all demands then due with interest and expenses, and transfer the shares sold to the purchaser, who is entitled to a certificate.
-- The text joins the two remedies with "or" and "shall" attaches to the sale; this rule says only that the stockholder is exposed to either (Fork F11).
-- src:560 | When any stockholder fails to pay any installment or call upon such stockholder’s stock which may have been properly demanded by the directors, at the time when such payment is due, the directors may collect the amount of any such installment or call or any balance thereof remaining unpaid, from the said stockholder by an action at law, or they shall sell at public sale such part of the shares of such delinquent stockholder as will pay all demands then due from such stockholder with interest and all incidental expenses, and shall transfer the shares so sold to the purchaser, who shall be entitled to a certificate therefor.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 164 (src:560)
GIVEN `the stockholder failed to pay an installment or call, properly demanded by the directors, when it was due` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 164 the directors may collect the amount by an action at law or sell the delinquent stockholder's shares at public sale` `the stockholder failed to pay an installment or call, properly demanded by the directors, when it was due` MEANS
    `the stockholder failed to pay an installment or call, properly demanded by the directors, when it was due`

-- Notice of the time and place of the sale and of the sum due on each share shall be given by advertisement at least 1 week before the sale, in a newspaper of the county in this State
-- where the corporation's registered office is located, and mailed to the delinquent stockholder at the last known post-office address at least 20 days before the sale.
-- src:561 | Notice of the time and place of such sale and of the sum due on each share shall be given by advertisement at least 1 week before the sale, in a newspaper of the county in this State where such corporation’s registered office is located, and such notice shall be mailed by the corporation to such delinquent stockholder at such stockholder’s last known post-office address, at least 20 days before such sale.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 164 (src:561)
GIVEN `the day of the sale` IS A DATE
      `the day the advertisement appeared` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was mailed to the delinquent stockholder` IS A DATE
      `the notice states the time and place of the sale and the sum due on each share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advertisement appeared in a newspaper of the county in this State where the corporation's registered office is located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was mailed to the delinquent stockholder at the last known post-office address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 164 the notice of the sale is as the section requires` `the day of the sale` `the day the advertisement appeared` `the day the notice was mailed to the delinquent stockholder` `the notice states the time and place of the sale and the sum due on each share` `the advertisement appeared in a newspaper of the county in this State where the corporation's registered office is located` `the notice was mailed to the delinquent stockholder at the last known post-office address` MEANS
        `the notice states the time and place of the sale and the sum due on each share`
    AND `the advertisement appeared in a newspaper of the county in this State where the corporation's registered office is located`
    AND `the notice was mailed to the delinquent stockholder at the last known post-office address`
    AND (`the day the advertisement appeared` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in weeks` 1) `before` `the day of the sale`))
    AND (`the day the notice was mailed to the delinquent stockholder` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 20) `before` `the day of the sale`))

-- If no bidder can be had to pay the amount due, and the amount is not collected by an action at law, which may be brought in the county where the corporation has its registered office,
-- within 1 year from the date of the bringing of the action, the stock and the amount previously paid in by the delinquent stockholder are forfeited to the corporation.
-- No action brought at all is a case the text does not address (the year runs from the bringing of the action): NOTHING.
-- src:562 | If no bidder can be had to pay the amount due on the stock, and if the amount is not collected by an action at law, which may be brought within the county where the corporation has its registered office, within 1 year from the date of the bringing of such action at law, the said stock and the amount previously paid in by the delinquent stockholder on the stock shall be forfeited to the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 164 (src:562)
GIVEN `no bidder can be had to pay the amount due on the stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the action at law was brought, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the amount was collected by the action, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day as of which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164 the stock and the amount previously paid in are forfeited to the corporation` `no bidder can be had to pay the amount due on the stock` `the day the action at law was brought, if it was` `the day the amount was collected by the action, if it was` `the day as of which the question is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the action at law was brought, if it was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST brought THEN
        JUST (    `no bidder can be had to pay the amount due on the stock`
              AND (`the day as of which the question is asked` GREATER THAN (`the date` (`period in years` 1) `after` brought))
              AND (    CONSIDER `the day the amount was collected by the action, if it was`
                       WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                       WHEN JUST collected THEN (collected GREATER THAN (`the date` (`period in years` 1) `after` brought))))

§ `Section 165: revocability of preincorporation subscriptions`

-- Unless otherwise provided by the terms of the subscription, a subscription for stock of a corporation to be formed is irrevocable, except with the consent of all other subscribers or the corporation,
-- for a period of 6 months from its date. The last day of the 6 months is inside the period (Fork F10). The section says nothing of a subscription for a corporation already formed: NOTHING.
-- src:566 | Unless otherwise provided by the terms of the subscription, a subscription for stock of a corporation to be formed shall be irrevocable, except with the consent of all other subscribers or the corporation, for a period of 6 months from its date.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 165 (src:566)
GIVEN `the subscription is for stock of a corporation to be formed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of the subscription provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all other subscribers consent to the revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation consents to the revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the subscription` IS A DATE
      `the day the revocation is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165 the subscription is irrevocable on the day of the revocation` `the subscription is for stock of a corporation to be formed` `the terms of the subscription provide otherwise` `all other subscribers consent to the revocation` `the corporation consents to the revocation` `the day of the subscription` `the day the revocation is made` MEANS
    IF `the subscription is for stock of a corporation to be formed`
    THEN JUST (    (NOT `the terms of the subscription provide otherwise`)
               AND (NOT (`all other subscribers consent to the revocation` OR `the corporation consents to the revocation`))
               AND (`the day the revocation is made` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in months` 6) `after` `the day of the subscription`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 166: formalities required of stock subscriptions`

-- A subscription for stock of a corporation, whether made before or after its formation, shall not be enforceable against a subscriber unless in writing and signed by the subscriber or by the subscriber's agent.
-- The section is a bar only: that it is in writing and signed does not by this section make it enforceable.
-- src:570 | A subscription for stock of a corporation, whether made before or after the formation of a corporation, shall not be enforceable against a subscriber, unless in writing and signed by the subscriber or by such subscriber’s agent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 166 (src:570)
GIVEN `the subscription is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscription is signed by the subscriber or by the subscriber's agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 166 the subscription is not enforceable against the subscriber` `the subscription is in writing` `the subscription is signed by the subscriber or by the subscriber's agent` MEANS
    NOT (    `the subscription is in writing`
         AND `the subscription is signed by the subscriber or by the subscriber's agent`)
